      "text": "Puno and Lake Titicaca"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "64f4afc8fcf5b23596d4309f538d40b5f9d9fd191436dd1c80bb7c9fd10e7a5d",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-work-8cfa443091a8",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, head to Lake Titicaca, which lies at almost **4,000 metres** above sea level.\n\nThere are more than **30 floating Uros Islands** on the lake, built from reeds.\n\nAymara communities live here. They make a living from fishing, tourism and handicrafts, and weave baskets, furniture and boats from reeds.\n\nDuring the excursion, you can take a ride in a traditional reed boat accompanied by a local resident.\n\nThe islanders maintain their own customs and traditions, and the Uros Islands are considered one of the most distinctive stops on this route through Peru.\n\nAfter the excursion, return to Puno for an overnight stay at a three-star hotel."
    },
